+#
+# CACTUS, Hao & Mou 2026. A training-free relaxed target distribution that
+# boosts the acceptance probability of the ACTUAL drafted token x as a
+# function of the target's own confidence in it, p(x) -- unlike lenience or
+# spec-casc-opt, the boost never reads q(x) or any other part of the drafter's
+# distribution:
+#
+#   gamma_x = min(p(x) + sqrt(2*alpha*p(x)*(1-p(x))), 1)
+#   accept  iff  gamma_x / q(x) >= u
+#
+# alpha >= 0 is (an approximation of) a bound on the reverse KL divergence of
+# the relaxed target from p; alpha=0 gives gamma_x = p(x) exactly, recovering
+# strict spec-dec bit-for-bit, which is why it is the safe default below.
+# Larger alpha boosts acceptance more.
+#
+# Naming: the paper's own symbol for this knob is delta, not alpha. It is
+# spelled alpha throughout this codebase's files/CLI/config-file names (they
+# predate noticing the mismatch, and every already-collected dataset's
+# on-disk tag uses it), so the code keeps that spelling rather than a
+# blast-radius rename across live data; this comment is the fidelity note.
+#
+# v2 correctness fix (this version): CACTUS does not just reweight the
+# accept/reject test for the drafted token x. It replaces the target
+# distribution seen by the WHOLE rejection-sampling machinery with a full,
+# proposal-conditioned distribution H_x over the entire vocabulary:
+#
+#   H_x(x)      = gamma_x
+#   H_x(y != x) = p(y) * (1 - gamma_x) / (1 - p(x))
+#
+# (a valid distribution: gamma_x + (1-gamma_x)/(1-p(x)) * sum_{y!=x} p(y) ==
+# gamma_x + (1-gamma_x) == 1). On rejection, the recovered token must be
+# sampled from r_x(y) ~ [H_x(y) - q(y)]_+, not from stock vLLM's [p(y) -
+# q(y)]_+. An earlier version of this patch implemented only the accept/reject
+# test and left recovery sampling on the unmodified strict residual -- a
+# hybrid of "CACTUS accept test + strict-SD recovery" with no correctness
+# guarantee from either paper. Data collected under that version is tagged
+# cactus_accept_only, not cactus, to keep the two honestly distinguished.
+# This version builds H_x in plain PyTorch (same style as spec-casc-opt's
+# defer_mask: a per-token pre-reduction before kernel launch, not new Triton
+# code) and substitutes it for target_probs in the call to
+# sample_recovered_tokens -- that function already computes normalized
+# [target_probs - draft_probs]_+ via a Gumbel-max trick, so feeding it H_x in
+# place of p makes the recovered-token distribution match the paper exactly,
+# with zero changes to vLLM's own recovery kernel.
+#
+# The alpha value comes from a file, not the environment, for the same reason
+# as every other patch here: vLLM spawns EngineCore with a sanitised
+# environment, so env vars never reach the sampler.
+_CACTUS_ALPHA_FILE = f"/tmp/lossy-token-eff-cactus-alpha-{os.getuid()}"
